<description>
Stamp the compact upper template into every marked lower mask cell as an expanded block image.

Input structure
- The grid has one solid grey separator row.
- Above it is a template region made of monochrome 2x2 blocks.
- Below it is a same-size mask containing only background and red marker pixels.

Rule
- Compress each 2x2 block in the upper region to one color, giving a small tile.
- Build a blank output whose coarse cell grid is the lower mask and whose cell size is the tile size.
- For every red marker pixel in the lower mask, paste the tile into the corresponding output block.

Key insight
The top half encodes the motif at half resolution, while the lower red mask encodes which coarse cells receive that motif.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "upper 6x6 template region and lower red marker mask separated by a grey row",
  "transform": "compress each 2x2 block of the template to one cell; expand each lower mask pixel to a 3x3 output block, stamping the compressed tile only at red marker positions and leaving other blocks background",
  "grid_shape": "13x6 input -> 18x18 output",
  "symbol_instructions": "upper template region encodes the 3x3 tile; lower red mask encodes the coarse output positions that receive the tile"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid:
    input: 13 rows x 6 cols [observed, fixed across all examples]
    structure: top template (6x6) | grey separator row | mask (6x6)
  separator: single row of all GREY (color 5), at row 6
  template:
    size: 6x6 (even rows x even cols) [observed]
    content: composed of 2x2 monochrome blocks; each block is a single color
    compressed_tile: 3x3 (template / 2 in each dimension)
    tile_non_bg_cells: 4-7 of 9 cells
    tile_distinct_non_bg_colors: 2-4
    tile_colors: any color except GREY; RED (2) allowed
  mask:
    size: same as template (6x6)
    content: only BLACK (bg=0) and RED (2)
    red_count: 5-12 cells
    red_connected_components: 1-3
    at_least_one_red: required
  output: 18x18 (mask_rows * tile_h x mask_cols * tile_w)
  transform: |
    For each RED cell (r,c) in mask, stamp the 3x3 tile at
    output[r*3:(r+1)*3, c*3:(c+1)*3]. Non-red mask cells -> bg block.

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input-first; both components are simple)
  steps:
    1. Create a 3x3 tile with 4-7 non-bg cells using 2-4 random non-GREY colors.
    2. Expand tile to 6x6 template by repeating each cell as a 2x2 block.
    3. Create a 6x6 mask with 5-12 RED cells (rest BLACK), ensuring >=1 RED.
    4. Assemble input as template (6 rows) + grey separator row + mask (6 rows) = 13x6.
```
</generation_spec>
